# .trivyignore — accepted-risk vulnerability suppressions for Trivy.
#
# Policy
# ------
# 1. Every entry MUST have a one-line justification comment ABOVE it
#    explaining what makes the CVE non-applicable HERE (not in the abstract).
# 2. Every entry MUST have an `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` expiry. On expiry, the CVE
#    reappears and must be re-triaged. There are no permanent ignores.
# 3. Suppressions are reviewed before every release.
# 4. When the volume justifies it, migrate from this file to OpenVEX
#    documents (machine-readable, scanner-portable). See
#    https://github.com/openvex/spec.
#
# Format
# ------
#   # <one-line justification — what makes this CVE non-applicable HERE>
#   <CVE-ID or GHSA-ID> exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Example
# -------
#   # urllib3 SOCKS proxy parsing — we don't use proxies in this app
#   CVE-2024-37891 exp:2026-12-01

# (no active suppressions yet)
